<%#
  What the password has to be, ticked as it is typed.

  Takes `for` (the id of the password box) and `rules` (from
  `passwordRules()`). The rules are rendered by the server, so **without the
  script the box still says what is required** - it is a plain list then,
  and `passwordProblems()` refuses anything that does not meet it either way.
  The script only adds the ticking; it decides nothing.

  Each row carries its own test name, so the script never has to parse the
  wording, and a service desk that turns a rule off simply has one row fewer.
-%>
<ul class="pw-rules" data-pw-rules="<%= locals.for %>" aria-label="What the password needs">
  <% rules.forEach(function (rule) { %>
    <li class="pw-rule" data-rule="<%= rule.test %>"<%- rule.min ? ' data-min="' + rule.min + '"' : '' %>>
      <%# aria-hidden: the row's text says it, and the state is announced below. -%>
      <span class="pw-rule__mark" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <span class="pw-rule__label"><%= rule.label %></span>
    </li>
  <% }); %>
</ul>
